{"name":"Vanilla Frost","hex":"#fde9c5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vanilla","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tropical climbing orchid of the genus Vanilla (especially Vanilla planifolia), bearing podlike fruit yielding an extract used in flavoring food or in perfumes.","The fruit or bean of the vanilla plant."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of vanilla.","Standard, plain, default, unmodified, basic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vanilla"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vanilla","blocks":[{"text":"Vanilla is a spice derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla, primarily obtained from the seed pods of the flat-leaved Mexican and Central American vanilla (V. planifolia)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla","wikidata":"Q13241"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330p